# groovedraft.part -- A groove that ends against a wall in a drafted floor
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jakob Kastelic

# A block along y whose faces lean in by a draft of 1 degree toward
# y = 0, so that its floor, the face on top, leans too; a groove cut
# into the floor from the end at y = 30 to a wall at y = 5, its walls
# drawn by 1.5 degrees the other way and its bottom corners round, as
# cones.  The edges where the groove meets the floor take rounds of
# 0.3: along its two walls, and across its end at the wall, where they
# meet in pairs at the two corners of the floor.
profile blk along y 0 0 0 40 0 0 40 10 0 0 10 0
extrude b from 30 to 0 blk draft 1
profile g along y 15 7 1 25 7 1 25 12 0 15 12 0
extrude gr from 31 to 5 g draft 1.5
subtract part b gr
round 0.3 gr b
